.TH LT-QWWAD_EF_DISPERSION "1" "September 2016" "lt-qwwad_ef_dispersion (Quantum Wells, Wires and Dots) 1.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lt-qwwad_ef_dispersion \- compute the dispersion relation for a set of energy subbands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lt-qwwad_ef_dispersion
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compute the dispersion relation for a set of subbands.
.SH OPTIONS

Generic options:
.TP
\fB\-h\fR [ \fB\-\-help\fR ]
display a help message
.TP
\fB\-v\fR [ \fB\-\-version\fR ]
display the version of the program
.HP
\fB\-c\fR [ \fB\-\-config\fR ] arg (=qwwad.cfg) name of the configuration file to be used
.SS "Program-specific options:"
.HP
\fB\-\-wffileprefix\fR arg (=wf_e) Prefix of wavefunction filenames.
.TP
\fB\-\-wffileext\fR arg (=.r)
File extension for wavefunction files.
.TP
\fB\-\-energyfile\fR arg (=Ee.r)
Filename of energy file.
.TP
\fB\-\-nkbt\fR arg (=5)
Maximum energy to print out for the subband
[multiple of kT].
.TP
\fB\-\-Te\fR arg (=100)
Carrier temperature [K].
.TP
\fB\-\-nk\fR arg (=100)
Number of k\-space points to print out
.TP
\fB\-\-disp\-prefix\fR arg (=dr_e)
Filename prefix to which dispersion curves will be
written
.TP
\fB\-\-disp\-ext\fR arg (=.r)
Filename extension to which dispersion curves will
be written
.TP
\fB\-\-relative\fR
Output dispersion relative to subband minima. If
not specified, the dispersion is given relative to
the band edge.
.TP
\fB\-\-mass\fR arg (=0.067)
In\-plane effective mass (relative to free
electron).
.TP
\fB\-\-alpha\fR arg (=0)
In\-plane non\-parabolicity parameter [1/eV].
.TP
\fB\-\-vcb\fR arg (=0)
Conduction band edge [eV].
.SS "Configuration options:"
.TP
\fB\-V\fR [ \fB\-\-verbose\fR ]
display lots of information about calculation
.SH FILES
.SS Input files:
   'E*.r'    Energy of each state:
             Column 1: state index.
             Column 2: energy [meV].

   'wf_*i.r' Wave function amplitude at each position:
             Column 1: position [m].
             Column 2: wave function amplitude [m^{-1/2}].

.SS Output files:
   'dr_*i.r' Dispersion relation for subband i
             Column 1: In-plane wave-vector [1/m]
             Column 2: Energy [meV]

In each case, the '*' is replaced by the particle ID and the 'i' is replaced by the number of the state.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compute the dispersion relation up to 10 kT with a carrier temperature of 10 K:
    qwwad_ef_dispersion --nkbt 10 --Te 10

Compute the non-parabolic dispersion relation using 1000 data points and dispersion of 0.7 eV^{-1}:
    qwwad_ef_dispersion --nk 1000 --alpha 0.7
